        "question_yNAhFi": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Your right to cancel (UK and EU customers)",
            "answer": "<p>If you are a consumer in the UK or the European Union, you have the right to cancel your order for any reason within 14 days of the day you (or someone you nominate) receive the products.</p><p>To cancel, email us at <a href=\"mailto:help@stendigcalendars.com\">help@stendigcalendars.com</a> with a clear statement that you wish to cancel, including your order number. You may use the model cancellation form at the end of these terms, but you do not have to.<br/><br/>If you cancel:</p><ul><li>You must return the products to us within 14 days of telling us you wish to cancel. Our Returns Policy explains how.</li><li>You are responsible for the cost of returning the products unless they are faulty or not as described.</li><li>We will refund the price you paid, including standard delivery charges, within 14 days of receiving the products back or receiving proof that you have sent them, whichever is earlier. If you chose a premium delivery option, we refund only the cost of our standard option.</li><li>Original delivery charges are refunded as required by law for UK and EU consumers exercising this cancellation right. For customers in other countries returning under our goodwill policy, we refund the product price only, and original delivery charges are not refunded.</li><li>We may reduce your refund to reflect any diminished value caused by handling beyond what is necessary to inspect the products, for example if a calendar is returned with pages removed, marked, or hung.</li></ul><p>This cancellation right is in addition to your legal rights if a product is faulty, described in section 8.</p><p>We extend a comparable goodwill returns period to customers in other countries. See our Returns Policy for details.<br/><br/><strong>Returns outside the 14-day window.</strong> We may, at our discretion, accept returns after the 14-day period has expired. Any such return is a goodwill gesture, not an entitlement. If accepted, we will refund the product price only. Original delivery charges will not be refunded, return postage remains your responsibility, and the products must be returned unused and in resaleable condition. This does not affect your statutory rights in respect of faulty goods, which apply regardless of the 14-day window.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_NqVMQE": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Faulty or incorrect products",
            "answer": "<p>If a product arrives damaged, faulty, or not as described, or if you receive the wrong item, contact us at <a href=\"mailto:help@stendigcalendars.com\">help@stendigcalendars.com</a> with your order number and photographs of the issue, and we will put it right with a replacement or a full refund, including delivery costs. We cover the cost of returning faulty or incorrect items.</p><p>Nothing in these terms affects your statutory rights. If you are in the UK, the Consumer Rights Act 2015 gives you rights where goods are faulty or not as described. If you are in the EU, you have a legal guarantee of at least two years under EU consumer law. Local mandatory consumer protections in your country of residence continue to apply.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_gHCwnX": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Our liability",
            "answer": "<p>If we fail to comply with these terms, we are responsible for loss or damage you suffer that is a foreseeable result of our breach, but we are not responsible for loss that is not foreseeable or for business losses.</p><p>We do not exclude or limit our liability where it would be unlawful to do so, including for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for your statutory rights as a consumer.</p>"
